  "notes": "Keeps a missing IR reading visible through repair until qualified direct recovery; shows a localized CHECK for a missing thermistor with fresh ADC evidence. Adds discrete curtain scrolling and the Settings pattern, root LED up/down controls, and a native flashlight with atomic On/Off, brightness, automatic, and mode preferences; removes the WLED rectangle. Adds smooth accepted-frame fades, including sleep and hibernate. Automatic IR uses valid range at or below 1 m as a low-IR-ambient proxy; this does not claim visible lux. Adds early OTA curtain collapse and early panel behavior. Lost-link or idle 20 s safe aborts, and severe slow transfer below 1024 B/s for 30 s, keep a localized fault and Desktop behavior. The old SW6106 hardware diagnostic remains paused. Hardware acceptance remains pending; no hardware success claim is made.",
